d_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.02648509639908551,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":55.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.0025,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":1.7,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Legence Corp. provides engineering, installation, and maintenance services for mission-critical systems in buildings in the United States. The company operates through two segments, Engineering & Consulting, and Installation & Maintenance. The Engineering & Consulting segment designs HVAC and other MEP systems for buildings, develops strategies to help reduce energy usage and make buildings more sustainable and provides program and project management services for client's installation and retrofit projects. This segment also offers engineering & design and program and project management services. The Installation & Maintenance segment fabricates and installs HVAC systems, process piping and other MEP systems in new and existing industrial, commercial and institutional buildings and provides ongoing preventative and corrective maintenance services, emergency repair, and break-fix services, as well as facility energy analysis, automation, optimization, and system certification and testing. It serves data centers, technology, life sciences, healthcare, education, mixed-use, state and local government, and other markets. The company was founded in 1914 and is based in San Jose, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jeffrey  Sprau | CEO & Director | Age 59 | Compensation: $2.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 7K people. Revenue per employee of $364K ranks in the above the sector median among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $31K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $10K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Legence Corp. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $5.7B market cap on $2.6B of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 21% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $219M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 9 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 0.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 68% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6807040229723108},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $1776.3M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 25% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Legence Corp. (LGN) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/legence-corp-lgn-q3-2026-052935000.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794548032.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"What LGN (LGN) Said on Its Q3 Earnings Call","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/lgn-lgn-said-q3-earnings-201454864.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794514494.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.791,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"LGN (NASDAQ:LGN) and Southland (NASDAQ:SLND) Critical Contrast","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/lgn-nasdaqlgn-and-southland-nasdaqslnd-critical-contrast.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794446105.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.876,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Legence Stock Trades Lower Despite Strong Q3 Earnings, High